# Commits and Naming

## Conventional Commits

Format: `type(scope): subject`

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `test`, `docs`, `chore`, `perf`, `ci`

```
feat(event): add ingest-time idempotency replay cache
fix(endpoint): return 404 instead of 500 for an unknown endpoint id
test(event): add outbox row creation assertion to ingestion test
```

## Branch naming

- `feature/<ticket-or-short-desc>` — new functionality
- `fix/<ticket-or-short-desc>` — bug fixes
- `refactor/<scope>` — structural changes
- `chore/<scope>` — tooling, deps, CI

## Semantic naming (mandatory)

Name by **domain and layer**, never generic:

```
# ❌ BAD
utils/Helpers.java
common/Service.java
DataProcessor.java

# ✅ GOOD
event/application/IngestEventUseCase.java
event/domain/Event.java
endpoint/infrastructure/EndpointRepositoryAdapter.java
```

## Test coverage

- Minimum **80%** line coverage on new/changed application and domain code.
- Every use case and domain state-machine rule must have a unit test.
- Every REST endpoint requires an integration test (MockMvc against a `docker compose`-provided Postgres + Redis, contract-validated against `openapi.yaml` — see `docs/adr/0012-contract-test-tooling.md` and `docs/adr/0014-docker-compose-test-seam.md`). Run `docker compose -f back_java/docker-compose.test.yml up -d` before `mvn test`.
